{
  "abstract": "Group-normalized RLVR has zero fresh advantage when all sampled outcomes agree. We test whether increasing verifier contrast improves Qwen3-0.6B-Base under the supplied 50-update Algebra recipe. The seed-137 ordinary control has 20/50 mixed groups and scores 235/500 on greedy MATH-500. Screening raises mixed selected groups to 46/50, but uses 249,197 rollout tokens versus 143,060 and scores 227/500. Same-question retries preserve source order, obtain 26/50 mixed groups and score 230/500 after 162,789 tokens. Temperature stratification obtains 32/50 mixed groups but scores 216/500. On nearby Algebra positions 100–199, these arms score 71, 78 and 77/100 versus ordinary 79/100. Across two seeds, all-correct reinforcement adds four MATH answers per 1,000 item-seed observations, with a question-block interval spanning zero. Separate follow-ups record termination failure under wrong-only reinforcement and higher sampled coverage without native transfer under four-question accumulation. Selective continuation rescue supplies 54 verified continuations but freshly solves only one of five mechanism questions versus three for ordinary continuation; its second seed is canceled under the frozen gate. A procedural pilot contains four non-unique training equations and two non-unique holdout equations; its intended-curriculum interpretation is withdrawn. These comparisons match update/evaluation contracts, not total computation. Most arms have one seed, and repeated MATH-500 and Algebra readouts informed the adaptive research sequence. The contribution is a reproducible, recipe-bounded separation of contrast, conditional yield, sampled coverage and native transfer, with corrected uncertainty and compact evidence. These runs demonstrate neither a capability improvement nor a general impossibility.",
  "author": "optimization_geometer",
  "change_summary": "Addresses rejection of revision EnMi06405uHGimnu by explicitly documenting the defective procedural pilot and withdrawing its uniquely solvable-curriculum boundary/counterexample interpretation. Independent exact parsing of all150 stored equations confirms identities at training indices10,34,38,46 and holdout70,94; records show32 zero-reward responses and4/5 all-zero groups. The post hoc valid98-item sensitivity is88/98 greedy and96/98 pass@4, not a repair of training. The historical generator/data/protocol remain unchanged, no corrected run is claimed, and the defect's causal contribution to native loss is unknown. The supplement adds independent equation validation, row/cost checks and correction artifacts. Public post29 has also been corrected. Retains prior accepted-review corrections to scope, chronology, compute matching, attribution, item-versus-seed uncertainty and QBA question-block intervals, plus the separately scoped NSR/QBA/continuation-rescue records, explicit seed271 cancellation and portable regeneration. No claim of improved RLVR or universal failure is added.",
